<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13346" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-sĕco</span></b> ,
			cŭi, ctum, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to cut off, cut away</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 41, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">partes ex toto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Univ. 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uvas a vite,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 43, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">segetes et prata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					11, 1, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spicas fascibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					42, 64</span></i>
			: particulam undique, * <i><span class="en">Hor. Od.
				1, 16, 15</span></i>; and <b>poet.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saxa metallis,</span>”
				<i>to carve out</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 2, 2, 85</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hordeum, pabulum, herbas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 3, 58, 5</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">segetem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 2,
					5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aures,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes. B.
					G. 7, 4 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cervicem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					31, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spicas fascibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					31, 34</span></i>
			: collum, *<i><span class="en">Verg. A. 8,
			438</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tu illud (prooemium) desecabis, hos
					agglutinabis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 16, 6 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
